input.prompt:
Follow-up on the same repo/session: <workspace>

An independent review found that the current fix can DUPLICATE Set-Cookie values. Repro: middleware does `c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', 'mw=1; Path=/')` (so `this.#res` exists), then handler returns `c.json(...)` / `c.text(...)`. `#newResponse` (src/context.ts:610) builds the new response with `new Headers(this.#res.headers)`, so `_res` already contains `mw=1; Path=/`. The setter then appends `this.#res`'s cookies again → `['mw=1; Path=/', 'mw=1; Path=/']`.

REQUIRED CHANGE in `src/context.ts` (`set res`, around lines 414-430)
Keep preserving both sides, but dedupe: only append previous `this.#res` cookies that are not already present on `_res`. Do not drop cookies that exist only on the new response. Keep the rest of the semantics (skip `content-type`; other headers overwritten via `set`; set-cookie skipped in the entries loop; body preserved; `finalized = true`). Suggested:

```ts
  set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
    if (this.#res && _res) {
      const cookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
      _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
      for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
        if (k === 'content-type' || k === 'set-cookie') {
          continue
        }
        _res.headers.set(k, v)
      }
      const newCookies = new Set(_res.headers.getSetCookie())
      for (const cookie of cookies) {
        if (!newCookies.has(cookie)) {
          _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
        }
      }
    }
    this.#res = _res
    this.finalized = true
  }
```

TESTS in `src/context.test.ts` — strengthen so duplication and old-bug regressions are both caught:
1. Keep the two existing updated tests, but also add a test that exercises the `c.json()`/`c.text()` copy path and fails on BOTH the original bug and the duplicate bug. Example:
```ts
  it('Should merge middleware and handler cookies without duplicating them', () => {
    c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', 'middleware=1; Path=/')

    const res = c.json({ ok: true }, 200, {
      'Set-Cookie': 'handler=2; Path=/',
    })
    c.res = res

    const cookies = c.res.headers.getSetCookie()
    expect(cookies.length).toBe(2)
    expect(cookies).toEqual(
      expect.arrayContaining(['middleware=1; Path=/', 'handler=2; Path=/'])
    )
  })
```
   (Note: on the ORIGINAL code this yields only the middleware cookie; on the no-dedupe fix it yields 3 with a duplicate. Both fail the length assertion.)
2. Strengthen the existing `'Should keep previous cookies in response headers'` test (around line 464) to assert the exact cookie list (length 2, contains both, and `cookies.length` exact) rather than only `includes`, so duplicates cannot pass silently.
3. Do not remove existing coverage. Keep style consistent.

CONSTRAINTS
- Only modify `src/context.ts` and `src/context.test.ts`.
- Never run `git add`/`git commit`; leave changes unstaged.
- Edit files with your file-editing tools, not shell redirection.

VERIFY
Run exactly: `pnpm exec vp test --run src/context.test.ts`
Then also run: `pnpm exec vp test --run src/compose.test.ts src/hono.test.ts`
And: `pnpm exec vp fmt --check src/context.ts src/context.test.ts` and `pnpm exec vp lint src/context.ts src/context.test.ts`

REPORT BACK
- Final diff of both files with line numbers.
- Test results (pass/fail counts) for all commands.
- Confirmation the new regression test fails with the old dedupe-less behavior (explain by inspection if you don't revert).
- Any remaining edge cases/concerns.

